MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze feels like a natural follow-up to Old Sock because I want more of Clapton's relaxed blues and roots sound.",
    "Croz and Standing in the Breach appeal through their songwriting, while several other choices correctly connect with the blues and roots side of my recent listening."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Endless River misses my current desire for songs with vocals; mostly instrumental atmosphere does not offer the blues or roots feel I want today.",
    "The Wild Feathers asks me to explore an unfamiliar artist when I am more inclined to choose someone familiar, and the live albums and reissues are less appealing for this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in Hendrix seems to have been taken as a broad desire for classic rock, even though heavier rock is less appealing than relaxed blues today.",
    "Familiar artists alone are not enough to make me choose an album; a live recording or reissue can fit my taste without fitting what I want now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to Old Sock matters especially when it leads to relaxed, vocal-led blues and roots music.",
    "I rarely act on several recommendations at once: an album can appeal to me and still be something I save for another visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in familiar rock and roots artists, but only a few capture the relaxed, vocal-led blues sound I want right now."
}
